-driven approach has many advantages compared to others. This"}]}, {"type": "incorrect", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "ones"}]}, {"type": "post_question", "contents": {"type": "", "content": "copies, process, integrates and restructures data."}}, {"type": "objective", "content": "secondary_1"}], "responses": [{"selected": 0, "correct": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0}, {"selected": 0, "correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": "one"}], "id": 1}], "id": 0}, {"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Some other approaches require to process data from local sources. These "}]}, {"type": "incorrect", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "one"}]}, {"type": "post_question", "contents": {"type": "", "content": "are not necessary for the update-driven approach."}}, {"type": "objective", "content": "secondary_1"}], "responses": [{"selected": 0, "correct": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0}, {"selected": 0, "correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": "ones"}], "id": 1}], "id": 1}, {"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "The update-driven approach is very common among software programmers. This is the best approach compared to other "}]}, {"type": "incorrect", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "one"}]}, {"type": "post_question", "contents": {"type": "", "content": "."}}, {"type": "objective", "content": "secondary_1"}], "responses": [{"selected": 0, "correct": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0}, {"selected": 0, "correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": "ones"}], "id": 1}], "id": 2}], "stimuli_ids": []}, {"template_override": 1, "id": 11, "type": "MT1", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " What can we ask about integrating heterogeneous approaches? "}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Quiz"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!"}}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Move the words up or down <span class=\"sena-icon sena-icon-vertical-drag\"></span> to complete each sentence."}]}], "questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "What approach is the most popular "}]}, {"type": "objective", "content": "secondary_1"}], "responses": [{"selected": 0, "correct": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0}, {"selected": 0, "correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": "if we talk about efficiency?"}], "id": 1}], "id": 0}, {"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "What do you do "}]}, {"type": "objective", "content": "secondary_1"}], "responses": [{"selected": 0, "correct": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0}, {"selected": 0, "correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": "if the approach you are using doesn't work?"}], "id": 1}], "id": 1}, {"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the both approaches give you many advantages, "}]}, {"type": "objective", "content": "secondary_1"}], "responses": [{"selected": 0, "correct": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0}, {"selected": 0, "correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": "which one do people think is better?   "}], "id": 1}], "id": 2}], "stimuli_ids": []}, {"template_override": 1, "id": 12, "type": "RSLT", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": []}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Quiz"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!"}}], "questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "responses": [{"selected": 0, "correct": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0}, {"selected": 0, "correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 1}], "id": 0}], "stimuli_ids": []}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0}, {"title": "", "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "type": "audio", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "enpe7n3le03ob07re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n3le03ob07re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe7n3le03ob07re2img01.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Jacquelyn</span>: Hey, Blake. Are you nervous about the conference? It's my first time talking in front of so many engineers and I am very anxious. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Blake</span>: Don't worry, Jacquelyn. Out of all my colleagues, you are the smartest one. At this point, we know a lot about data warehousing. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Jacquelyn</span>: But what do we do if they ask something we don't know? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Blake</span>: Mmm, you stumped me. Let's practice a little more. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Jacquelyn</span>: Ok, do you know if we can implement data warehouses in any domain? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Blake</span>: Well, there are three domains where we can use the information gathered in a warehouse. The first one has to do with tuning production strategies, the second one helps us with customer analysis, and the last one manages everything related to operations analysis.", "id": 0}, {"time": "54000", "image": "enpe7n3le03ob07re2img02.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Jacquelyn</span>: Excellent. It's your turn to ask me something. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Blake</span>: All right, if we need to integrate heterogeneous databases, what approaches do we have to use? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Jacquelyn</span>: We use the query-driven and the update-driven approaches. Those ones are the most common. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Blake</span>: Good! If they ask you to describe the query-driven approach, what do you think it's important to mention? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Jacquelyn</span>: Well, that approach is common to build wrappers and integrators, which people also call mediators. The process of the query-driven approach includes issuing a query to a client side so that a metadata dictionary can translate it for heterogeneous sites. After that, the query goes to the local query processor and gets into a global answer set. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Blake</span>: Great, do you know if that approach has any disadvantages?  <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Jacquelyn</span>: Certainly! It's somehow inefficient, complex, and expensive if we compare it to other approaches.  Now it's your turn, Blake. You have to explain the update-driven approach.", "id": 1}, {"time": "130000", "image": "enpe7n3le03ob07re2img03.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Blake</span>: In that approach, we integrate the information from multiple heterogeneous sources in a warehouse for direct querying and analysis. The update-driven is capable of providing high performance and it does not require interfaces to process data from local sources. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Jacquelyn</span>: I feel better now. We are ready!", "id": 2}]}}], "_data": []}], "id": 0}], "type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Query-Driven vs. Update-Driven Approach,        Advantages and Disadvantages"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about heterogeneous databases."}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe common activities at work to a visitor using short sentences in familiar spoken and written situations. Understand information about data and its structure in simple spoken and written situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations.   Describes common activities related to Software Programming through the use of appropriate expressions, grammar and vocabulary in written or spoken situations according to the abilities related to this level."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n3le03ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Zero Conditional in Questions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">zero conditional</span> to talk about situations that represent facts or rules."}, {"type": "text", "content": "To create questions using zero conditional, you can use the following grammatical structure: <br/><br/>   <div class=\"center_text\"> (Wh Word) + Question in Simple Present + <span class=\"strong\">if</span> + Statement in Simple Present + ? </div><br/><br/>  Examples: <br/>  <span class=\"italic\">What do you do <span class=\"strong\">if</span> you need to use a data warehouse? <br/> Does she have to analyze the data <span class=\"strong\">if</span> she wants to know about customers' preferences? </span><br/><br/>  Remember that we can reverse the order of the questions and start by using the conjunction <span class=\"strong\">if</span>; make sure you separate the two clauses with a comma (,).<br/> <br/>  Examples: <br/>  <span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\">If</span> you need to use a data warehouse, what do you do? <br/> <span class=\"strong\">If</span> she wants to know about customer preferences, does she have to analyze the data? </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "But what do we do if they ask something we don't know?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Do you know if we can implement data warehouses in any domain? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If we need to integrate heterogeneous databases, what approaches do we have to use? "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Pronouns One - Ones"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the pronouns <span class=\"strong\">one</span> and <span class=\"strong\">ones</span> to avoid repeating a noun in a sentence or paragraph. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">one</span> to replace a singular noun when you need to mention it a second time in a sentence or paragraph. You can use <span class=\"strong\">one</span> after <span class=\"italic\">this, that</span> or an adjective. <br/><br/>  Example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">A</span>: Do I click on the right or left key? <br/> <span class=\"strong\">B</span>: Click on the left <span class=\"strong\">one</span>.</span><br/><br/>  In the previous example, <span class=\"strong\">one</span> replaces the noun <span class=\"italic\">key</span>. <br/><br/>  You use <span class=\"strong\">ones</span> to replace plural nouns when you need to mention them a second time in a sentence or paragraph. <br/><br/>  Example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">A</span>: Do you need me to download new programs or update the current <span class=\"strong\">ones</span>?<br/> <span class=\"strong\">B</span>: Download new <span class=\"strong\">ones</span>, please. </span><br/><br/>  In the previous example, <span class=\"strong\">ones</span> replace the noun <span class=\"italic\">programs</span>. <br/>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Out of all my colleagues, you are the smartest one."}, {"type": "example", "content": "There are three domains where we can use the information gathered in a warehouse. The first one has to do with tuning production strategies."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We use the query-driven and the update-driven approaches. Those ones are the most common."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "warehouse "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a place where you can store goods or data"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We integrate the information from multiple heterogeneous sources in a warehouse. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n3le03ob07aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "domain "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a specific area or field"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are three domains where we can use the information gathered in a warehouse."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n3le03ob07aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "heterogeneous"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "dissimilar or different"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The process of the query-driven approach includes issuing a query to a client side so that a metadata dictionary can translate it for heterogeneous sites."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n3le03ob07aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "processor"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "component that interprets and executes signals"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: After that, the query goes to the local query processor and gets into a global answer set."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n3le03ob07aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "query"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a search or question"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: After that, the query goes to the local query processor and gets into a global answer set."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n3le03ob07aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "source "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the origin of something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: In that approach, we integrate the information from multiple heterogeneous sources in a warehouse for direct querying and analysis."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n3le03ob07aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for more information about Query-Driven and Update-Driven approaches."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a comparative chart contrasting each one"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a short paragraph describing briefly their advantages and disadvantages using the grammar studied. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss your work with your partners "}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I can Look for more information about Query-Driven and Update-Driven approaches."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can Make a comparative chart contrasting each one"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can Write a short paragraph describing briefly their advantages and disadvantages using the grammar studied. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can Discuss my work with my partners"}]}]}